            <title>[LU-20552] MDD: mdd_lmm_oi/gen ignore LOV_MAGIC_SEL and LOV_MAGIC_DEFINED</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20552</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;During work on &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20534" title="FLR-EC: Stripe replacement: swapping individual stripes between components" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20534"&gt;LU-20534&lt;/a&gt; an unrelated issue in dependent code was found.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;mdd_lmm_oi()  and  mdd_lmm_gen()  only matched  LOV_MAGIC_COMP_V1 .&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SEL: Layouts with extension components use  LOV_MAGIC_SEL  (same composite blob as COMP_V1). During MDT migrate,  mdd_xattrs_migrate_prep()  calls  mdd_set_lmm_oi() ; with SEL that was a no-op, so the LOV kept the old MDT FID in  lmm_oi .&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;DEFINED: When swap applies a layout onto a layout-less file,  mdd_swap_layouts()  ORs  LOV_MAGIC_DEFINED  on the incoming LOV before  mdd_set_lmm_gen() . The gen helper did not mask that bit, so generation updates failed. ( mdd_lmm_oi()  callers never pass DEFINED; masking there is for symmetry only.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: Treat  LOV_MAGIC_SEL  like COMP_V1; mask  LOV_MAGIC_DEFINED  when matching magic.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
